{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Overestimation Bias: The model consistently forecasts a monotonic upward trend regardless of recent price action, leading to significant overestimation during the initial 10-15 day horizon when prices are actually correcting or volatile.",
    "Failure to Capture Mean Reversion: The model ignores the strong mean-reverting behavior observed in the true data (dropping from ~90 to ~78 and rebounding), instead projecting a smooth, linear increase that fails to account for sharp drawdowns.",
    "Sentiment Lag/Ineffectiveness: Positive sentiment signals (0.20) in the history do not trigger immediate upward adjustments in the forecast; the model remains anchored to a long-term bullish trajectory even when sentiment is neutral or prices are falling.",
    "Overshoot Correction Required: Forecasts must be adjusted downward by 5-10 EUR in the short term (days 1-10) to align with the observed volatility and subsequent price dips, rather than assuming continuous growth.",
    "Horizon-Specific Lag: The model exhibits a lag in reacting to the mid-term recovery (days 15-20), where true prices spike significantly above the forecast; the model's linear projection is too conservative to capture the magnitude of the rebound."
  ]
}
